1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,127
Four drug boats.

2
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:04,030
One Coast Guard helicopter.

3
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:07,341
And one rule for the marksman in the open door:

4
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:09,384
shoot until the engines stop.

5
00:00:09,834 --> 00:00:13,240
February 2025, about 110 miles south of the

6
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,666
Galápagos Islands.

7
00:00:14,666 --> 00:00:17,994
A drone launched from a Coast Guard cutter

8
00:00:17,994 --> 00:00:21,400
picks up the boats, running together across

9
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:22,271
open water.

10
00:00:22,721 --> 00:00:25,814
The Coast Guard's own account calls it four

11
00:00:25,814 --> 00:00:27,252
boats in 15 minutes.

12
00:00:27,252 --> 00:00:29,554
Nearly 11,000 pounds of cocaine.

13
00:00:29,554 --> 00:00:32,215
Eight suspected smugglers in custody.

14
00:00:32,665 --> 00:00:35,376
How does a helicopter stop a speedboat in the

15
00:00:35,376 --> 00:00:36,582
middle of the ocean?

16
00:00:36,582 --> 00:00:39,233
And why does the Coast Guard keep a squadron

17
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:40,921
of aerial marksmen to do it?

18
00:00:41,371 --> 00:00:43,926
This is the case file on the Coast Guard's

19
00:00:43,926 --> 00:00:45,083
helicopter snipers.

20
00:00:47,683 --> 00:00:48,877
Start on the ship.

21
00:00:49,327 --> 00:00:52,767
In the winter of 2024 into 2025, the Coast

22
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:56,452
Guard cutter Stone was on a long counter-drug

23
00:00:56,452 --> 00:00:59,891
patrol in the Eastern Pacific, off Mexico,

24
00:00:59,891 --> 00:01:02,021
Ecuador and the Galápagos.

25
00:01:02,471 --> 00:01:04,831
It had already been a busy trip.

26
00:01:04,831 --> 00:01:08,151
Three days before Christmas, Stone's crew had

27
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:11,249
seized about 12,220 pounds of cocaine in a

28
00:01:11,249 --> 00:01:12,135
single case.

29
00:01:12,585 --> 00:01:15,182
On board, the ship carried a drone, and a

30
00:01:15,182 --> 00:01:18,034
helicopter crew from a small Coast Guard unit

31
00:01:18,034 --> 00:01:18,921
called HITRON.

32
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:22,326
The drone did a lot of the hunting.

33
00:01:22,326 --> 00:01:26,125
On January 30, about 715 miles off Mexico, it

34
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:29,840
found a suspicious boat carrying about 3,800

35
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,360
pounds of cocaine.

36
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:35,284
The next day, 630 miles out, it found another.

37
00:01:35,284 --> 00:01:38,683
Its infrared camera picks the boat out on the

38
00:01:38,683 --> 00:01:39,514
dark water.

39
00:01:39,514 --> 00:01:42,989
More than 2,500 pounds of cocaine were seized.

40
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:46,418
By February, the ship and the helicopter crew

41
00:01:46,418 --> 00:01:48,405
had worked six cases together.

42
00:01:48,405 --> 00:01:51,252
They had gone through a tough certification

43
00:01:51,252 --> 00:01:54,365
side by side, and built trust the ordinary way:

44
00:01:54,365 --> 00:01:56,815
board games, swim calls, port visits.

45
00:01:57,265 --> 00:01:59,883
On February 19, the operations officer,

46
00:01:59,883 --> 00:02:02,501
Lieutenant Commander Steven Naylor, was

47
00:02:02,501 --> 00:02:05,119
watching the drone's feed in the ship's

48
00:02:05,119 --> 00:02:08,072
command center, when a go-fast boat appeared

49
00:02:08,072 --> 00:02:09,012
on the screen.

50
00:02:09,012 --> 00:02:10,086
Then three more.

51
00:02:10,536 --> 00:02:13,175
Stone had three small boats to put boarding

52
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:14,526
teams on four targets.

53
00:02:14,526 --> 00:02:17,533
So two of the teams would have to share one boat.

54
00:02:17,983 --> 00:02:20,558
The commanding officer, Captain Jonathan

55
00:02:20,558 --> 00:02:22,424
Carter, kept the goal modest.

56
00:02:22,424 --> 00:02:25,578
One boat, he told the crew, would count as a win.

57
00:02:26,378 --> 00:02:29,071
To understand what happened next, you need to

58
00:02:29,071 --> 00:02:30,986
know who was in that helicopter.

59
00:02:31,436 --> 00:02:34,093
HITRON stands for Helicopter Interdiction

60
00:02:34,093 --> 00:02:35,259
Tactical Squadron.

61
00:02:35,259 --> 00:02:38,175
It is based in Jacksonville, Florida, and the

62
00:02:38,175 --> 00:02:40,638
Coast Guard calls it its only airborne

63
00:02:40,638 --> 00:02:41,804
use-of-force unit.

64
00:02:42,254 --> 00:02:45,738
Its crews fly MH-65 Dolphin helicopters, and

65
00:02:45,738 --> 00:02:49,222
they deploy for weeks at a time aboard Coast

66
00:02:49,222 --> 00:02:51,598
Guard cutters, far out at sea.

67
00:02:52,048 --> 00:02:54,891
On a case, three people in that helicopter

68
00:02:54,891 --> 00:02:55,703
matter most.

69
00:02:55,703 --> 00:02:56,786
One pilot flies.

70
00:02:56,786 --> 00:03:00,170
A second pilot coordinates and tracks the targets.

71
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:03,013
And in the door sits a precision marksman.

72
00:03:03,463 --> 00:03:05,760
The usual sequence goes like this.

73
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,179
First, warning shots.

74
00:03:07,179 --> 00:03:10,084
If the boat keeps going, the marksman fires

75
00:03:10,084 --> 00:03:12,786
again, this time to disable its engines.

76
00:03:13,236 --> 00:03:16,065
Once the boat is stopped, a boarding team from

77
00:03:16,065 --> 00:03:18,832
the cutter moves in, and the helicopter stays

78
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:20,553
overhead to watch over them.

79
00:03:21,003 --> 00:03:23,718
HITRON's commanding officer, Captain Dan

80
00:03:23,718 --> 00:03:26,569
Broadhurst, describes the job in a way you

81
00:03:26,569 --> 00:03:27,723
might not expect.

82
00:03:28,523 --> 00:03:31,452
The squadron runs its own shooting program.

83
00:03:31,452 --> 00:03:34,449
One marksman joined with only basic firearms

84
00:03:34,449 --> 00:03:37,718
experience, and went on to become an instructor.

85
00:03:38,168 --> 00:03:40,855
One precision marksman, Petty Officer First

86
00:03:40,855 --> 00:03:43,604
Class Taylor Wolf, explained the difference:

87
00:03:43,604 --> 00:03:46,416
we're shooting from an aerial platform, which

88
00:03:46,416 --> 00:03:48,728
is very different than anywhere else.

89
00:03:49,178 --> 00:03:51,112
The pilots come from everywhere.

90
00:03:51,112 --> 00:03:53,649
One of them, Lieutenant Andy Gilliam, flew

91
00:03:53,649 --> 00:03:56,187
Black Hawks in the Army before joining the

92
00:03:56,187 --> 00:03:58,665
Coast Guard through its direct commission

93
00:03:58,665 --> 00:03:59,631
aviator program.

94
00:04:00,081 --> 00:04:01,553
Back to the four boats.

95
00:04:02,003 --> 00:04:04,901
The plan was called Operation Shoot and Move.

96
00:04:04,901 --> 00:04:07,670
The helicopter would disable the boats from

97
00:04:07,670 --> 00:04:10,568
behind, and Stone's small boats would follow,

98
00:04:10,568 --> 00:04:12,499
putting boarding teams aboard.

99
00:04:12,949 --> 00:04:14,305
It did not go to plan.

100
00:04:14,305 --> 00:04:17,140
The smugglers circled, dumped their cargo into

101
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:18,496
the sea, and split up.

102
00:04:18,946 --> 00:04:21,596
They scattered like ants, said the pilot

103
00:04:21,596 --> 00:04:22,523
tracking them.

104
00:04:22,523 --> 00:04:25,305
The other pilot, Lieutenant Commander Adam

105
00:04:25,305 --> 00:04:27,358
Ownbey, said plan B was simple:

106
00:04:27,358 --> 00:04:28,484
you make it work.

107
00:04:28,484 --> 00:04:29,677
Embrace the chaos.

108
00:04:30,127 --> 00:04:32,949
In the door, the precision marksman, Petty

109
00:04:32,949 --> 00:04:35,771
Officer Second Class Ryan Teal, worked the

110
00:04:35,771 --> 00:04:36,779
mounted weapon.

111
00:04:36,779 --> 00:04:39,535
Every one of those boats had two engines.

112
00:04:39,985 --> 00:04:41,734
Teal described his rule.

113
00:04:42,534 --> 00:04:46,150
For the first time on a case, he had to reload.

114
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:49,611
By his own estimate, he fired either 33 or 36

115
00:04:49,611 --> 00:04:50,150
rounds.

116
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,444
The fourth boat stopped and its crew complied.

117
00:04:53,444 --> 00:04:55,854
But a communications mix-up delayed the

118
00:04:55,854 --> 00:04:58,574
boarding team, so the helicopter stayed with

119
00:04:58,574 --> 00:05:00,861
it, until it was running low on fuel.

120
00:05:01,311 --> 00:05:04,122
When it was over, Naylor and Carter confirmed

121
00:05:04,122 --> 00:05:06,557
the result the simplest way they could.

122
00:05:06,557 --> 00:05:08,181
Each held up four fingers.

123
00:05:08,631 --> 00:05:10,227
Naylor admitted it afterward:

124
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,705
honestly, none of us thought it would happen.

125
00:05:13,155 --> 00:05:15,213
The Coast Guard's tally:

126
00:05:15,213 --> 00:05:19,157
four go-fast boats, eight suspected smugglers,

127
00:05:19,157 --> 00:05:22,158
and about 10,885 pounds of cocaine.

128
00:05:22,608 --> 00:05:25,299
Stone's patrol still was not over.

129
00:05:25,299 --> 00:05:28,861
On March 10, about 270 miles southeast of the

130
00:05:28,861 --> 00:05:32,423
Galápagos, the ship's HITRON crew spotted one

131
00:05:32,423 --> 00:05:34,085
more suspicious boat.

132
00:05:34,535 --> 00:05:38,140
On the helicopter's camera, it runs, throwing

133
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:39,342
up a long wake.

134
00:05:39,342 --> 00:05:41,584
Stone's crew interdicted it:

135
00:05:41,584 --> 00:05:44,628
about 3,980 pounds of cocaine, and two

136
00:05:44,628 --> 00:05:46,951
suspected smugglers detained.

137
00:05:47,401 --> 00:05:50,608
In August 2026, at a ceremony in Washington,

138
00:05:50,608 --> 00:05:53,961
the White House drug policy office gave HITRON

139
00:05:53,961 --> 00:05:57,023
and Stone's crew its Maritime Interdiction

140
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:59,647
Award, for that one day in February.

141
00:06:00,097 --> 00:06:03,126
That day was one case among more than a thousand.

142
00:06:03,576 --> 00:06:05,944
The squadron dates back to 1999.

143
00:06:05,944 --> 00:06:09,199
That August, a Jacksonville HITRON crew made

144
00:06:09,199 --> 00:06:12,455
its first drug interdiction, by shooting out

145
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:15,267
the outboard motors of a go-fast boat.

146
00:06:15,717 --> 00:06:18,750
By its twentieth year, it counted more than

147
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:21,854
500 interdictions, and more than $20 billion

148
00:06:21,854 --> 00:06:23,759
worth of narcotics stopped.

149
00:06:24,209 --> 00:06:27,267
The thousandth came on August 25, 2025,

150
00:06:27,267 --> 00:06:30,874
working with the cutter Midgett in the Eastern

151
00:06:30,874 --> 00:06:31,501
Pacific:

152
00:06:31,501 --> 00:06:34,950
about 3,606 pounds of suspected cocaine, and

153
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:37,773
six suspected smugglers apprehended.

154
00:06:37,773 --> 00:06:41,066
The boat would not comply, and the aircrew

155
00:06:41,066 --> 00:06:42,791
used force to stop it.

156
00:06:43,241 --> 00:06:45,110
It was a record stretch.

157
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:48,694
From October 2024 to that September, the Coast

158
00:06:48,694 --> 00:06:51,888
Guard says, HITRON crews interdicted $3.3

159
00:06:51,888 --> 00:06:55,472
billion in drugs, about three times the unit's

160
00:06:55,472 --> 00:06:57,342
historic annual average.

161
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,911
Then came the cutter Munro.

162
00:06:59,911 --> 00:07:03,522
It left Alameda, California, in November 2025.

163
00:07:03,522 --> 00:07:06,975
Somewhere in the Eastern Pacific, its HITRON

164
00:07:06,975 --> 00:07:10,507
aircrew used warning shots and disabling fire

165
00:07:10,507 --> 00:07:12,469
to stop one go-fast boat.

166
00:07:12,919 --> 00:07:13,673
On board:

167
00:07:13,673 --> 00:07:15,767
22,052 pounds of cocaine.

168
00:07:15,767 --> 00:07:19,453
The Coast Guard called it the single largest

169
00:07:19,453 --> 00:07:22,301
maritime drug seizure in 18 years.

170
00:07:22,301 --> 00:07:25,485
Six suspected smugglers were detained.

171
00:07:25,935 --> 00:07:29,178
By then the Coast Guard had launched Operation

172
00:07:29,178 --> 00:07:31,787
Pacific Viper in the Eastern Pacific.

173
00:07:31,787 --> 00:07:34,959
By its own count, the operation was averaging

174
00:07:34,959 --> 00:07:37,497
about 1,600 pounds of cocaine a day.

175
00:07:37,947 --> 00:07:41,019
To mark the year, HITRON painted one of its

176
00:07:41,019 --> 00:07:42,305
helicopters black.

177
00:07:42,305 --> 00:07:45,520
The Coast Guard calls it the Blackfin scheme,

178
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:48,378
for the unit's role in seizing more than

179
00:07:48,378 --> 00:07:50,235
511,000 pounds of cocaine.

180
00:07:50,685 --> 00:07:52,802
The method has not changed.

181
00:07:52,802 --> 00:07:54,291
Here it is in 2026.

182
00:07:54,741 --> 00:07:57,561
Most of these chases start long before the

183
00:07:57,561 --> 00:07:58,972
helicopter takes off.

184
00:07:58,972 --> 00:08:01,658
A joint task force in Key West, Florida,

185
00:08:01,658 --> 00:08:03,605
watches the smuggling routes.

186
00:08:03,605 --> 00:08:06,627
Once an interdiction is close, control shifts

187
00:08:06,627 --> 00:08:07,903
to the Coast Guard.

188
00:08:08,353 --> 00:08:08,786
May 8.

189
00:08:08,786 --> 00:08:11,890
About 90 miles off Cartagena, Colombia, the

190
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:14,921
crew of the cutter Tahoma went after three

191
00:08:14,921 --> 00:08:18,025
suspected smuggling boats at once, with two

192
00:08:18,025 --> 00:08:20,407
small boats and a HITRON aircrew.

193
00:08:20,857 --> 00:08:23,564
Two of the boats stopped when Coast Guard

194
00:08:23,564 --> 00:08:24,819
crews told them to.

195
00:08:24,819 --> 00:08:27,790
The third kept going, and the helicopter crew

196
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,563
used precision sniper fire on its engines.

197
00:08:31,013 --> 00:08:34,293
The suspected smugglers aboard jumped into the sea.

198
00:08:34,293 --> 00:08:36,994
The aircrew dropped flotation devices, and

199
00:08:36,994 --> 00:08:39,888
they were rescued, with no injuries reported.

200
00:08:40,338 --> 00:08:43,935
About 6,085 pounds of cocaine, worth nearly

201
00:08:43,935 --> 00:08:45,107
$45.8 million.

202
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:48,704
Commander Nolan Cuevas, Tahoma's commanding

203
00:08:48,704 --> 00:08:52,469
officer, called interdicting three vessels at

204
00:08:52,469 --> 00:08:55,314
once a testament to the unwavering

205
00:08:55,314 --> 00:08:58,493
professionalism of the crews involved.

206
00:08:58,943 --> 00:09:03,316
Six days later, at Port Everglades, Florida,

207
00:09:03,316 --> 00:09:07,788
Tahoma's crew offloaded about 8,185 pounds of

208
00:09:07,788 --> 00:09:11,465
narcotics, worth about $61.6 million.

209
00:09:11,915 --> 00:09:16,099
And in November 2026, Tahoma was back at the

210
00:09:16,099 --> 00:09:19,617
same pier, with another 3,622 pounds.

211
00:09:20,067 --> 00:09:23,202
Every one of these chases ends in the same two

212
00:09:23,202 --> 00:09:23,679
places.

213
00:09:23,679 --> 00:09:25,315
A pier, and a courtroom.

214
00:09:25,765 --> 00:09:29,380
Stone's patrol ended in March 2025.

215
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:33,203
At Port Everglades, Florida, its crew

216
00:09:33,203 --> 00:09:37,645
offloaded about 45,600 pounds of narcotics,

217
00:09:37,645 --> 00:09:40,847
worth more than $517.5 million.

218
00:09:41,297 --> 00:09:44,249
It was the haul from 14 interdictions.

219
00:09:44,249 --> 00:09:47,278
35 suspected smugglers were transferred

220
00:09:47,278 --> 00:09:51,239
ashore, to face federal prosecution in U.S. courts.

221
00:09:51,689 --> 00:09:53,506
None of them is named here.

222
00:09:53,506 --> 00:09:56,534
A charge is an accusation, and anyone charged

223
00:09:56,534 --> 00:09:59,966
is presumed innocent unless proven guilty in court.

224
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:02,358
Stone was not alone out there.

225
00:10:02,358 --> 00:10:05,271
The cutter Mohawk worked the same waters, and

226
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:07,796
its commanding officer, Commander David

227
00:10:07,796 --> 00:10:09,803
Ratner, summed up the strategy.

228
00:10:10,253 --> 00:10:11,277
In his words.

229
00:10:12,077 --> 00:10:14,251
Captain Carter credited the partnership

230
00:10:14,251 --> 00:10:16,258
between the ship and the helicopter.

231
00:10:17,058 --> 00:10:20,148
Since 1999, the method has barely changed.

232
00:10:20,148 --> 00:10:22,796
Find the boat from the air. Warn it.

233
00:10:22,796 --> 00:10:25,591
And if it runs, take away its engines.

234
00:10:26,041 --> 00:10:29,419
HITRON passed 1,000 interdictions in 2025.

235
00:10:29,419 --> 00:10:31,189
The boats keep coming.

236
00:10:31,189 --> 00:10:33,039
So does the helicopter.

237
00:10:33,489 --> 00:10:34,941
Case file 015.

238
00:10:34,941 --> 00:10:36,497
Closed for now.
